  "helpTitle": "Questions",
  "helpHowTitle": "How does it work?",
  "helpHowBody": "The app receives the sound other apps play, runs it through an on-device neural network (DPDFNet) that keeps human voices and removes everything else, and plays the cleaned voice. At the same time it silences the original sound of those apps.",
  "help100Title": "Is the music removed 100%?",
  "help100Body": "Instrumental music is removed almost completely: in tests, music alone went from full volume to silence (−60 to −100 dB), and speech over music stays clear. Singing is a human voice, so the voice of a singer can remain (the instruments are still removed).",
  "helpAppsTitle": "Which apps work?",
  "helpAppsBody": "YouTube, Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, Snapchat and most video apps. Apps that forbid audio capture (Netflix, Spotify, some browsers like Chrome, a few games) keep playing unchanged — the app shows them as “blocks processing”.",
  "helpAdbTitle": "Why the one-time activation?",
  "helpAdbBody": "Android lets apps capture other apps' sound, but not silence them. The activation gives the app the right to see which app is playing so it can mute its original sound. Without it, you would hear the music and the cleaned voice at the same time.",
  "helpDelayTitle": "The sound is slightly late",
  "helpDelayBody": "Cleaning needs about 50 ms plus the audio buffers. Choose “Low” delay in the settings. Bluetooth headphones add their own delay.",
  "helpBatteryTitle": "Battery",
  "helpBatteryBody": "The model runs only while sound is playing. When the video is paused the engine idles. Light quality uses about 4× less processing.",
  "helpPrivacyTitle": "Privacy",
  "helpPrivacyBody": "Everything happens on the phone and the app cannot access the internet at all. Android shows a screen-sharing icon while it runs, because capturing other apps' sound goes through the same system as screen sharing; the app never looks at your screen.",
  "helpTroubleTitle": "I hear the music and the voice together",
  "helpTroubleBody": "Check that the activation is done (Settings › Setup). If the app is listed as “blocks processing”, Android does not allow cleaning it.",
  "helpCutTitle": "Words are cut or the voice drops",
  "helpCutBody": "When the music is as loud as the voice, the AI can take parts of words for music. Voice protection (Settings) listens for speech with two separate detectors and keeps the words, while music alone is still removed. If words are still cut, set it to Strong, or choose Full quality if your phone can run it.",
  "helpSilentTitle": "An app has no sound after closing No Mosi9a",
  "helpSilentBody": "If No Mosi9a is force-stopped while a video plays, Android can keep that video muted. Open No Mosi9a or pull down the quick settings: it restores the sound automatically. Stopping it with its own button never causes this.",
